  "funFact": "The axolotl is a tiger salamander — it is a neotenic form of Ambystoma, retaining juvenile features (external gills, aquatic lifestyle) into adulthood. The olm is a blind cave salamander that also has external gills and lives permanently in water, looking strikingly similar to an axolotl — but it belongs to a completely different salamander family (Proteidae). The axolotl looks nothing like a tiger salamander, yet they are essentially the same animal.",
